  "2026-10-14T07:54:47.624Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus, fresh flag searches and open/in-progress reads; full closed normalization owner metadata/history read. GH1467 identifies a residual pre-existing mismatch, not a new14 regression, with published14 acceptance still pending. No exact existing owner found. Keep related completed work completed and this new scope open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-14T16:06:32.149Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: retain optional value arity before normalization and carry it through SDK contracts, Commander, JSON help and recovery, without a second flag-name registry. Incorporate issue clarification comments through2026-10-14T09:58Z. Use the existing public parity verifier with actual extension observations plus independent exact dispatch expectations; bind recurring required pre-publication acceptance to candidate tarball digest. Pair with pm-gh1466; only these edited work items are in_progress."
  "2026-10-14T16:20:26.157Z","harness:codex","Verified official public2026.10.14 tarball against registry SHA512 integrity; unchanged semantic echo fixture reproduces false-to-true with leftover positional false. Candidate source integration now passes37 declared cases across nested/flattened commands: exact boolean values, optional/required arity, list ordering, short forms, remaining operands, required-flag presence and safe refusals. Independent seeded lost-optionality and false-to-true controls are required to fail for their named semantic assertions. Full coverage, complete static and npm/Bun/npx/bunx packed acceptance are running; none is claimed passed yet."
  "2026-10-14T16:21:41.039Z","harness:codex","Operational intake complete: all24 currently open GitHub issues now have canonical PM-link comments; reports1469-1472 are recorded under their proper owners without reopening delivered work or claiming planning containers. Both GitHub and local pnpm audit currently report zero known vulnerabilities. New registry updates are within the explicit seven-day cooldown; older incompatible major migrations remain with their existing PM owners. Latest pm-changelog2026.10.13 installed through the package-owned path, with no generator edits in this repo. No agent-browser skill found in the enabled host skill/plugin directories."
  "2026-10-14T16:23:20.870Z","harness:codex","The independently verified public2026.10.14 SDK also reproduces the second failure: --maybe [label] reports help takes_value=true/value_required=false while public SDK machine contracts report value_required=true. Both original bug signatures are now confirmed on an integrity-verified published artifact, not source reconstruction. Source and candidate acceptance are separate from the next future daily release. The new malformed-scalar validation enhancement is recorded as pm-extension-scalar-validation and remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-14T16:27:14.778Z","harness:codex","Candidate acceptance now also invokes the public PmClient.run extension action directly, with an independent literal expectation for explicit false values, optional presence, ordered list values and remaining operands. The packed receipt includes runtime name/version/platform/architecture, actual export resolution, the whole semantic fixture digest, the runner digest and exact candidate tarball SHA256. The SDK surface snapshot explicitly records the additive optional CliFlagContract.value_arity field and the shared helper exports; legacy core inference remains available when the field is absent."
  "2026-10-14T16:31:22.217Z","harness:codex","Chrome Computer Use also confirms the latest reviewed DeepScan branch inventory:0 open/confirmed findings,120 fixed, Issue-free, and0 new findings for prior PR1468. These are existing branch observations; the new PR will require its own exact-head analyzers and reviews. No hosted status was copied or manufactured. The baseline optionality probe and all source/packed receipts retain separate evidence scopes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T16:23:18.005Z","harness:codex","Scalar coercion and argv value arity are distinct contracts. Preserve the original extension declaration before canonicalizing aliases, and assert literal handler options/remaining arguments independently of help-contract agreement. A packed-candidate digest cannot establish a published-installed fix."
